# Trivy waivers. Empty by default: any known CVE or finding fails `make trivy-fs`.
# A waiver is allowed only for a finding with NO fixed version upstream, and every entry
# carries an expiry and a justification on the line above it:
#   # exp:YYYY-MM-DD <why it is not exploitable here> - <upstream tracking link>
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN
# W-1: golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained and has no upstream fix. It is linked only into
# the tfplugindocs documentation generator (tools/go.mod), which runs in development and CI on the
# provider's own schema and is never shipped. The provider binary (root go.mod) has no x/crypto
# requirement. Re-check when tfplugindocs moves to a release without it.
# exp:2027-01-20 not exploitable here - https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-5932
GO-2026-5932 exp:2027-01-20
